# OC-30: false-reject rate on full 1000x1000 matrices of synthetic full-entropy data.
# Row/column dependence INCLUDED (Hill comment 3.b). Cutoffs: printed-formula then corrected.
8-bit full entropy, 2000 matrices (1000x1000, rows AND columns, dependence included):
  cutoff   15 rejects  1664 of 2000 =  83.20%
  cutoff   19 rejects     4 of 2000 =   0.20%
4-bit full entropy, 2000 matrices (1000x1000, rows AND columns, dependence included):
  cutoff   99 rejects   233 of 2000 =  11.65%
  cutoff  104 rejects    18 of 2000 =   0.90%
2-bit full entropy, 2000 matrices (1000x1000, rows AND columns, dependence included):
  cutoff  312 rejects    63 of 2000 =   3.15%
  cutoff  316 rejects    13 of 2000 =   0.65%
1-bit full entropy, 2000 matrices (1000x1000, rows AND columns, dependence included):
  cutoff  570 rejects    28 of 2000 =   1.40%
  cutoff  572 rejects    15 of 2000 =   0.75%
8-bit full entropy, 20000 matrices (1000x1000, rows AND columns, dependence included):
  cutoff   15 rejects 16499 of 20000 =  82.50%
  cutoff   18 rejects   304 of 20000 =   1.52%
  cutoff   19 rejects    53 of 20000 =   0.27%
